    "guide.learn.why.kicker": { "zh": "為什麼需要它？", "en": "Why it exists" },
    "guide.learn.why.note": { "zh": "維持<strong>核心市場曝險不減</strong>，用一檔 ETF 同時持有基礎曝險與分散化策略。", "en": "Keep <strong>full core market exposure</strong> while stacking base exposure and a diversifier in one ETF." },
    "guide.learn.why.p1": { "zh": "一般做法要加「替代策略」，得從股票或債券減碼（例如 60/40 改成 50/30/20）。替代策略落後時，投資人容易在股票創高時「砍掉它」——官方稱這是「用減法做分散」，容易產生行為摩擦。", "en": "Traditional diversification means trimming stocks or bonds (e.g. 60/40 → 50/30/20) to add alts. When alts lag, investors often sell them at stock highs—the classic behavioral friction of subtractive diversification." },
    "guide.learn.why.problem.label": { "zh": "減法分散", "en": "Subtractive mix" },
    "guide.learn.why.solution.label": { "zh": "報酬疊加", "en": "Return Stacking" },
    "guide.learn.why.title": { "zh": "傳統分散化的困境", "en": "The diversification dilemma" },
